## J. Limitations & Risks

- **OOD Brittleness (IEEE)**: The CNN-LSTM is purely data-driven. If TrustSense encounters a cooling failure or extreme current spike not present in the PyBaMM training data, the CNN-LSTM will likely confidently predict an incorrect, unsafe temperature.
- **Spatial Ignorance (IEEE)**: The IEEE model ignores thermal conduction from neighboring cells. If an adjacent cell goes into thermal runaway, this model won't predict the heat transfer.
- **Hardware Constraints**: The P CNN-LSTM requires 13 layers (including heavy dense and recurrent layers). Running this continuously for hundreds of cells on an edge device (Jetson Orin Nano) alongside an LLM is a major latency/OOM risk.

